@user Well, first of all, both of these are possibilities until history runs it course and we learn the truth.

But, no, option 1 is just how supply/demand economics works. AI is more productive and cheaper than humans. AI will achieve more than humans ever could, and in less time. Therefore, an explosion of goods and services + a deflation in the cost to procure those goods and services = universal high income. Every expert that isn't a complete doomer agrees with this.

We can't know the future, but there is actually far more certainty that AI will result in a worldwide economic boom than that AI will kill us all. Primarily because the first one is already happening, and the second one can't happen until several more milestones are reached.
